=== phase-032 [major] Reconcile the stdlib module list in SPEC.md with src/stdlib.rs
depends: phase-026
must_touch: ["src/","docs/"]
finding: src/stdlib.rs:7 declares `pub const MODULES: &[&str] = &["console", "csv", "files", "json", "network", "time"]` and src/analyzer.rs:270 rejects a bare receiver that is neither in scope nor in `stdlib::MODULES` with `Unknown variable`. SPEC.md §Standard Library documents four modules that are not in that list — `text` (SPEC.md:753-760), `math` (762-769), `list` (782-788) and `formats` (797-803) — so `text.uppercase("hi")` fails with `AnalyzerError: Unknown variable 'text'` and `formats.parse_json("{}")` with `Unknown variable 'formats'`. The functions those sections describe already exist as bare builtins at src/stdlib.rs:22-153 (`uppercase`, `lowercase`, `split`, `join`, `sqrt`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `json_parse`, `csv_parse`); they are registered under flat names, not under the module names SPEC.md prints. README.md:120-151 documents only files/time/network/json/csv, which agrees with src/stdlib.rs — so README and SPEC disagree with each other.
goal: Make src/stdlib.rs, SPEC.md and README.md agree on which module names exist, routing the builtins that already exist under the documented names or correcting the documents to the names the code really uses.

=== phase-050 [major] Reconcile SPEC.md's stdlib module names with src/stdlib.rs MODULES
depends: phase-041
must_touch: ["src/"]
finding: src/stdlib.rs:7 declares `pub const MODULES: &[&str] = &["bytes", "console", "csv", "files", "json", "list", "network", "sys", "time"]` and src/analyzer.rs rejects any other bare receiver as `Unknown variable`. SPEC.md's Standard Library section documents seven module headings that do not agree with it: `### text` (SPEC.md:950), `### math` (SPEC.md:959), `### formats` (SPEC.md:994) and `### console` (SPEC.md:942) — the last three of those names are absent from MODULES. Verified against the built binary, one call per documented module: `text.uppercase("hi")` fails with `AnalyzerError: Unknown variable 'text'`, `math.sqrt(9)` with `Unknown variable 'math'`, `formats.parse_json("{}")` with `Unknown variable 'formats'`, and `console.ask("n")` fails with `ParserError: Expected property name` because `ask` is a reserved keyword (that half is phase-049's work, not this phase's). `list.map([1,2,3], to (x) give back x*2 end)` DOES work and prints `[2, 4, 6]`, because `list` is in MODULES. The two names SPEC.md uses and MODULES omits are `text` (SPEC.md:952-957 documents uppercase, lowercase, split, join) and `math` (SPEC.md:960-966 documents PI, sqrt, random, round) — and `formats` (SPEC.md:995-800 documents parse_json, to_json, parse_csv), where `json` and `csv` are in MODULES and do work. SPEC.md:799 and SPEC.md:806-814 then build `catch error`/`might fail` examples on `formats.parse_json`, which is doubly unreachable. phase-032 owned this reconciliation and is `.blocked` — rbops/dispatch.sh:242 skips a `.blocked` id permanently and it has 0 commits on redblue main, so it will never run. phase-041 covers `text.split`/`text.join` specifically but explicitly defers the module-list reconciliation, so the name-level disagreement is still unowned.
goal: Make `src/stdlib.rs`, SPEC.md and README.md name the same set of modules, so no module the specification documents is rejected as an unknown variable.

=== phase-051 [blocker] Delete the uncommitted S3 work sitting in a checkout whose phase is marked .done
depends: 
must_touch: ["bootstrap/"]
finding: phases/phase-022/.done exists in the pipeline root, and the corresponding commit on redblue main is dff04f6 `resume phase-022: adopt preserved work`. But `git -C redblue status --short` shows SEVEN modified files with 941 insertions and 335 deletions that are NOT in any commit: bootstrap/compiler.rb (+143 -…), docs/BOOTSTRAP.md (+167), phases/phase-022/FINDINGS.md, phases/phase-022/REPORT.md, src/interpreter.rs (+33), src/runtime.rs (+1) and tests/bootstrap_selfhost_test.rs (+393). These are not stray edits: they are precisely the files phases/phase-022/REPORT.md claims to have changed — the REPORT's `What changed` table lists bootstrap/compiler.rb, src/interpreter.rs, src/runtime.rs, tests/bootstrap_selfhost_test.rs, docs/BOOTSTRAP.md and phases/phase-022/FINDINGS.md, and its Tests-added table lists four tests that appear nowhere in dff04f6's 13-file diff. So the phase's REPORT describes work that is not committed, the state store says the phase is done, and `cargo test` is green partly BECAUSE the working tree carries 393 lines of uncommitted test code. A green gate on an uncommitted tree is exactly the fake completion the reviewer contract (AGENTS.md section 5) is built to catch: the next `git checkout`, the next fresh CI clone, or the next phase that starts from a clean tree loses all of it. The S3 fixed point that phase-022 exists to prove is not in the commit history at all — `git log --oneline main | grep phase-022` prints exactly one line, the resume commit, and no test named in its REPORT is present in it.
goal: Get the S3 fixed-point work out of the working tree and onto main behind a commit, so the phase's REPORT describes history rather than an uncommitted checkout.

=== phase-078 [blocker] Make the checkpoint ancestry in redblue main detectable instead of a comment
depends: 
must_touch: ["tests/"]
finding: rbops/dispatch.sh:442-447 admits it in prose and nothing measures it, so the number can only grow silently: 'six of them are in redblue's history today, carrying unreviewed code.' Measured this audit: `git -C redblue log --oneline main | grep checkpoint` prints 4 lines - 7fdea15 and 074c95e `rbops: phase-019 checkpoint`, 563a351 `rbops: phase-018 checkpoint`, 286fccd `rbops: phase-016 checkpoint` - and `git -C redblue log --oneline main | grep -c "Merge remote-tracking branch"` prints 4, the real `git merge` commits that put them there (e97983a, d664d3c, 2179034, 255816e). rbops/dispatch.sh:439-486 now resumes with `git merge --squash`, so the recurrence path is closed and this is a measurement that has never existed, not a live bug. phase-051 is a different defect (uncommitted work, not ancestry) and does not cover it.
goal: Add an executable check that fails when any `rbops: phase-NNN checkpoint` commit that is an ancestor of redblue main is not on a hand-maintained acknowledgement list, and record in the repository that the four existing ones carry unreviewed code and were not rewritten.

=== phase-079 [blocker] Land phase-041's work behind a commit, or take back its `.done`
depends: 
must_touch: ["src/"]
finding: phases/phase-041/.done exists and `git -C redblue log --oneline main --grep='phase-041 '` prints nothing. The work is sitting in the working tree: `git -C redblue status --porcelain` reports ` M src/parser.rs`, `A tests/text_split_join_test.rs`, `A phases/phase-041/REPORT.md`, `A phases/phase-041/FINDINGS.md`, and `git -C redblue diff --stat HEAD` totals 1800 insertions and 17 deletions, of which tests/text_split_join_test.rs is 1235 lines that no commit contains. The state store says the phase is complete, its REPORT describes a change that exists in no commit, and `cargo test` is green partly because 1235 lines of test code were never committed. The next `git checkout`, the next fresh CI clone, or the next phase that starts from a clean tree loses all of it. This is the defect class phase-051 names, but phase-051 names phase-022 specifically, and phase-022's work has since landed as 054e0d6 - so phase-051's finding no longer reproduces and this is the live instance.
goal: Get phase-041's implementation onto redblue main behind a commit its own REPORT describes, so the gate is green from history rather than from an uncommitted working tree.

=== phase-080 [critical] Make `items at N` and `length of X` real, or strike them from SPEC.md
depends: 
must_touch: ["src/"]
finding: SPEC.md:319 `set first to items at 0`, SPEC.md:320 `set last to items at -1` and SPEC.md:327 `set count to length of items` are written as working syntax under `### List Operations`. None of them works. Verified against the built binary: after `set items to [1,2,3]`, `set first to items at 0` gives `AnalyzerError: Unknown variable 'at'` (src/analyzer.rs:436) and `set count to length of items` gives `AnalyzerError: Unknown variable 'of'`. The cause is src/parser.rs:664-667 - the `_` arm of `parse_statement_inner` falls through to `parse_expression()` and wraps whatever it finds as `Statement::Expr`, so `set first to items at 0` is not a parse error at all, it is THREE statements: `set first to items`, `at`, `0`. Two tools then make it worse: `rb format` prints those three lines back (verified - `rb format` on that file emits `set first to items` / `at` / `0`), and `rb lint` reports no diagnostic at all on a file `rb` cannot run (verified - lint prints only `Unused variable: 'first'` and exits 0). No corpus, example or module program uses either form, so nothing else in the suite notices.
goal: Either implement the two documented forms or correct SPEC.md, and stop the parser from silently turning an unconsumed line into stray expression statements.

=== phase-081 [major] Execute every ```redblue block in the five documents that define the language
depends: phase-080
must_touch: ["tests/"]
finding: 97 ```redblue blocks exist across the documents that define Redblue - SPEC.md 64, docs/GRAMMAR.md 9, PHILOSOPHY.md 9, HANDOUT.md 8, README.md 7 - and no test runs any of them. Every existing reference is a hand-quoted single example (tests/for_range_test.rs:2 cites SPEC.md:380-391, tests/formatter_test.rs:2008 cites SPEC.md:383). Measured this audit by extracting and running every block: 58 of 97 do not run, among them SPEC.md:319 and SPEC.md:327 (the phase-080 forms), SPEC.md:1068 (`LexerError: Unexpected character '\''` - Redblue has no single-quoted string), SPEC.md:1066 (`ParserError: Unexpected token Wait`, owned by phase-049) and HANDOUT.md:155 (`filter was called with arguments it cannot use`, owned by phase-077). Many of the 58 are fragments rather than defects - docs/GRAMMAR.md:526-532's example omits its `end` - so the first deliverable is an honest classification, NOT 58 features. The rotted examples are exactly the ones that cost an audit to find: `items at 0` sat in SPEC.md undetected until now.
goal: Build the test that extracts and classifies every documentation code block, so a documentation promise cannot rot unnoticed, and turn the first true classification into a report a human can act on.

=== phase-082 [major] Make every place the project states what works, true
depends: phase-081
must_touch: ["tests/"]
finding: Five documents state what Redblue does and all five are wrong somewhere. SPEC.md:1068 writes `json.parse('{"name": "Alice"}')` with single quotes and the lexer rejects `'` - `LexerError: Unexpected character '\''`, raised at src/lexer.rs:506 - because Redblue has no single-quoted string. SPEC.md:1073 states 'There is no `formats` module' while HANDOUT.md:149 and HANDOUT.md:154 document `formats.parse_json` and `formats.to_json`. HANDOUT.md:155-157 document `list.map` and `list.filter`, and `list.filter` answers `filter was called with arguments it cannot use`; both names are listed as known gaps at tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs:259-261. README.md:237 lists `src/vm.rs` in the project structure and that file does not exist - it was renamed to `src/interpreter.rs`. README.md:279 still marks self-hosting 'in progress' although bootstrap/compiler.rb is 2854 lines and tests/bootstrap_selfhost_test.rs already asserts stage-2 and stage-3 byte-identical output (edge_stage2_is_byte_identical_on_every_corpus_program, edge_the_self_compiled_compiler_compiles_itself_byte_identical). Worst of all, tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs:270-274 exempts console_clear, time_unix, csv_parse, network_get and network_post as 'documented but not implemented', and ALL FIVE work at runtime: `console.clear()` clears, `time.unix("2024-01-01 00:00:00")` answers 1704067200, `csv.parse("a,b\n1,2")` answers `[[a, b], [1, 2]]`, `json.parse` answers a record. An exemption list that is stale in the PERMISSIVE direction stops testing things that work.
goal: Correct every false statement in SPEC.md, README.md, PHILOSOPHY.md, HANDOUT.md and docs/GRAMMAR.md and shrink the stale KNOWN_GAPS list, so no document claims a capability the binary lacks and no gate-supporting test exempts a working builtin.
